  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY: ⟦{自動詞|じどうし}→自動詞：10977_jidoushi⟧ (intransitive). Pattern: X⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧Y⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧{似|に}る (X resembles Y) / X⟦と→と：00512_to⟧Y⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{似|に}る (X and Y are similar).\n\nASPECT: て⟦いる→いる：00495_iru⟧ is almost always used. {似|に}て⟦いる→いる：00495_iru⟧ = 'resembles' (state). The plain form {似|に}る is rarely used alone.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- X⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧{似|に}て⟦いる→いる：00495_iru⟧ (resemble X)\n- ⟦よく→よく：00601_yoku⟧{似|に}て⟦いる→いる：00495_iru⟧ (look very similar)\n- {似|に}た⟦ような→ような：noentry⟧ (similar—attributive)\n- ⟦{似合|にあ}う→似合う：02134_niau⟧ (to suit, look good on—related but different verb)\n- ⟦{似顔絵|にがおえ}→似顔絵：11456_nigaoe⟧ (portrait, likeness)\n\nGRAMMAR NOTE: Unlike many verbs, {似|に}る is almost exclusively used in the て⟦いる→いる：00495_iru⟧ form in modern Japanese. Saying X ⟦は→は：00079_ha⟧ Y ⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧{似|に}る sounds unnatural; X ⟦は→は：00079_ha⟧ Y ⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧{似|に}て⟦いる→いる：00495_iru⟧ is correct.\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- ⟦{似合|にあ}う→似合う：02134_niau⟧: to suit (a different verb meaning 'to look good on')",
